    "https://www.higheredjobs.com/institution/details.cfm?JobCode=179586707&Title=Director%20of%20Student%20Financial%20Services": {
      "title": "Director of Student Financial Services",
      "description": "Director of Student Financial Services - HigherEdJobs Your Privacy We use cookies and other similar technologies to enhance user experience, for website maintenance purposes, and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our website with advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal, then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Do Not Sell My Personal Information I understand Skip to main content Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Online/Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail Director of Student Financial Services Elms College in Chicopee, MA Apply Now Type: Full-Time Salary: $85,000 - $92,000 per year Posted: 1 day ago (Reposted Job: Initially posted on 09/10/2026) Category: Financial Aid Priority Report to: VP of Enrollment Management and Marketing Position Summary The Director of Student Financial Services provides strategic, operational, and regulatory leadership for Elms College's Student Financial Services department, overseeing Financial Aid and Student Accounts. The Director is responsible for ensuring the accurate, compliant, and fiscally responsible administration of federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid programs, as well as effective oversight of student account operations. The Director serves as the College's senior financial aid administrator and is accountable for financial aid compliance, financial aid budgeting and forecasting, reconciliation, and the responsible stewardship of institutional, federal, and state financial aid resources. The Director leads and develops the Student Financial Services team while fostering a culture of accountability, accuracy, collaboration, and exceptional student service. Working collaboratively across Enrollment Management, Finance, and other areas of the College, the Director develops strategies that support enrollment, retention, student success, and institutional financial sustainability. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Provide strategic and operational leadership for Student Financial Services, including Financial Aid and Student Accounts, establishing clear priorities, expectations, policies, and standards of accountability. Lead, supervise, develop, and evaluate Student Financial Services staff, ensuring appropriate training, cross-training, professional development, and accountability for performance. Oversee the administration of all federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid programs, ensuring funds are awarded, disbursed, reconciled, and reported accurately and in accordance with all applicable requirements. Maintain primary responsibility for financial aid regulatory compliance, including Title IV requirements, Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP), Return of Title IV Funds (R2T4), verification, consumer information requirements, and federal and state reporting. Develop, maintain, and enforce comprehensive financial aid policies, procedures, internal controls, and documentation to ensure consistent and compliant administration of financial aid programs. Lead preparation for financial aid audits, program reviews, and regulatory inquiries; monitor regulatory changes and ensure timely implementation of required institutional and operational changes. Provide leadership and direct oversight of the College's financial aid budget, including annual projections, forecasting, monitoring expenditures and commitments, and identifying and addressing actual or projected budget variances. Ensure financial aid commitments remain within approved funding levels and provide College leadership with timely and accurate reporting regarding expenditures, available resources, projected liabilities, and financial risk. Oversee the accurate and timely reconciliation of federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid funds in collaboration with Finance. Partner with Enrollment Management and Finance leadership to develop financial aid strategies that support enrollment, student affordability, net tuition revenue, and institutional financial sustainability. Oversee student account operations, including billing, payment plans, accounts receivable, refunds, collections, and reconciliations, in close collaboration with the Finance department. Develop coordinated Financial Aid and Student Accounts processes that provide students and families with a seamless, responsive, and student-centered financial services experience. Provide strategic analysis related to financial aid awarding, institutional aid, student affordability, and enrollment trends to support institutional decision-making. Serve as an escalation point and institutional subject matter expert for complex financial aid, student account, regulatory, and student financial services matters. Utilize data and technology to improve operational efficiency, monitor key performance indicators, strengthen compliance, and support strategic decision-making. Collaborate cross-divisionally to improve processes, enhance service, and address financial barriers that may affect student enrollment, retention, and persistence. Represent Student Financial Services on College committees, at institutional events, and with appropriate external agencies and professional organizations, including some evenings and weekends. Maintain current knowledge of financial aid regulations, industry standards, and emerging practices through ongoing professional development. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree required; master’s degree preferred. Progressively responsible experience in higher education financial aid administration, including experience with federal Title IV programs. Demonstrated expertise in federal and state financial aid regulations and compliance. Demonstrated experience managing financial aid budgets, including forecasting, monitoring expenditures, reconciliation, and financial reporting. Supervisory or management experience with demonstrated ability to lead, develop, and hold staff accountable. Experience with financial aid management systems, student information systems, and federal financial aid systems and reporting. Experience with Colleague preferred. Strong analytical, organizational, written, verbal, and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to manage complex priorities with a high degree of accuracy, sound judgment, and attention to detail. Elms College (also known as College of Our Lady of the Elms), a private, Catholic, co-educational liberal arts institution in Chicopee, Massachusetts, was founded in 1928 by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Springfield. The institution offers Associate's, Bachelor's, Master's, and Doctor of Nursing practice degrees. Dedicated to non-discriminatory educational practices, the College aims to eliminate barriers to equal access and treatment for its community. Elms College provides rigorous academic challenges and fosters a supportive community for students to thrive. Graduates leave Elms College richer, rooted in faith, educated, compassionate, responsive to civic and social obligations, and capable of adjusting to change without compromising principle. Elms College’s mission embodies the charism of the founders, the Sisters of St. Joseph, including embracing “the love of neighbor without distinction” and whose Catholic heritage guides our intellectual, social, educational, and community endeavors. Elms College is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants will not be discriminated against because of race, color, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, national origin, citizenship status, disability, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, medical condition, or any protected category prohibited by local, state or federal laws. Apply Now Related Searches: Financial Aid Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Email: jobs@elms.edu OR Apply through HigherEdJobs Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) Post Doctorate Adjunct/Part-Time Administrative/Staff Executive (Director, Asst/Assoc VP/Dean) Senior Executive (VP, Dean, President/Chancellor) Please type the characters to the left above (case sensitive). Close Job Seeker Login Email Password Keep me signed in Log In Forgot your password? Don't have an account? Sign Up (New) Terms and Conditions of Use (Updated) Privacy Policy"
