      "description": "Assistant Director of Student Financial Services - HigherEdJobs Your Privacy We use cookies and other similar technologies to enhance user experience, for website maintenance purposes, and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our website with advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal, then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Do Not Sell My Personal Information I understand Skip to main content Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Online/Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail Assistant Director of Student Financial Services Elms College in Chicopee, MA Apply Now Type: Full-Time Salary: $46,000 - $50,000 per year Posted: 22 days ago Application Due: Open Until Filled Category: Financial Aid Position Summary Reporting to the Director of Student Financial Services, the Assistant Director of Student Financial Services is responsible for administering federal, state, and institutional financial aid programs and providing high-quality financial aid counseling and service to students and families. The Assistant Director manages financial aid awarding and processing for assigned student populations, counsels’ students regarding financial aid eligibility and financing options, and supports the accurate and timely disbursement and reconciliation of financial aid funds. The Assistant Director works collaboratively with colleagues across Student Financial Services, Admissions, Finance, and other College offices to support students throughout the enrollment and financial aid process while ensuring compliance with all applicable federal, state, and institutional regulations and policies. Primary Duties and Responsibilities ·Provides comprehensive financial aid counseling to students and families through individual appointments, phone, email, virtual meetings, and walk-in service; Delivers responsive, student-centered customer service and assists students and families in navigating complex or sensitive financial circumstances. · Verifies eligibility and awards federal, state, and institutional financial aid to undergraduate and graduate students in accordance with applicable regulations, policies, and established procedures · Manages financial aid processing for assigned student populations, including verification, professional judgment documentation, awarding, revisions, and resolution of conflicting or incomplete information. · Utilizes the College's financial aid management system and federal systems to perform verification, process ISIR corrections, complete COD reporting, and facilitate the accurate and timely disbursement of financial aid funds. · Reviews student accounts and financial aid records to identify and resolve issues that may prevent or delay the disbursement of aid. · Assists the Associate Director and Director of Student Financial Services, when needed, with monthly and annual reconciliation of federal and state financial aid programs and works collaboratively with appropriate departments to research and resolve discrepancies. · Educates students and families regarding financial aid eligibility, FAFSA requirements, grants, scholarships, loans, satisfactory academic progress, financing options, and other financial aid policies and processes. · Responds to financial aid inquiries and assists with outreach to students regarding missing documentation, incomplete requirements, financial aid eligibility, and other action items. · Exercises appropriate professional judgment when reviewing individual student circumstances in accordance with federal regulations and institutional policy. · Maintains accurate and complete student records and documentation to support regulatory compliance, audits, and program reviews. · Participates in financial aid presentations, workshops, open houses, orientation programs, and other recruitment and student-focused events as needed, including some evening and weekend programs. · Collaborates with Admissions, Student Accounts, Registrar, Academic Affairs, and other College offices to resolve student issues and provide a coordinated student experience. · Maintains current knowledge of Title IV regulations, state financial aid requirements, institutional policies, and financial aid best practices through professional development, regulatory updates, and professional publications. · Protects the confidentiality of student information and ensures compliance with FERPA and other applicable regulations. · Supports the Director of Student Financial Services and SFS team with special projects, compliance initiatives, reporting, and other departmental priorities. · Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications · Bachelor's degree required. · Prior experience in financial aid, student financial services, higher education, or a related field strongly preferred. · Working knowledge of federal Title IV financial aid regulations and financial aid administration preferred. · Experience with financial aid management systems, student information systems, and federal financial aid systems preferred. · Strong customer service and interpersonal skills, with the ability to communicate complex financial information clearly and compassionately to students and families. · Strong attention to detail and demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines, and student cases accurately. · Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and work effectively with sensitive student and family financial information. · Strong written and verbal communication skills. · Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively as part of a student-centered team. · Ability and willingness to remain current on changing federal and state financial aid regulations and requirements. Elms College (also known as College of Our Lady of the Elms), a private, Catholic, co-educational liberal arts institution in Chicopee, Massachusetts, was founded in 1928 by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Springfield. The institution offers Associate's, Bachelor's, Master's, and Doctor of Nursing practice degrees. Dedicated to non-discriminatory educational practices, the College aims to eliminate barriers to equal access and treatment for its community. Elms College provides rigorous academic challenges and fosters a supportive community for students to thrive. Graduates leave Elms College richer, rooted in faith, educated, compassionate, responsive to civic and social obligations, and capable of adjusting to change without compromising principle. Elms College’s mission embodies the charism of the founders, the Sisters of St. Joseph, including embracing “the love of neighbor without distinction” and whose Catholic heritage guides our intellectual, social, educational, and community endeavors. Elms College is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants will not be discriminated against because of race, color, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, national origin, citizenship status, disability, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, medical condition, or any protected category prohibited by local, state or federal laws. Apply Now Related Searches: Financial Aid Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Email: jobs@elms.edu OR Apply through HigherEdJobs Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) Post Doctorate Adjunct/Part-Time Administrative/Staff Executive (Director, Asst/Assoc VP/Dean) Senior Executive (VP, Dean, President/Chancellor) Please type the characters to the left above (case sensitive). Close Job Seeker Login Email Password Keep me signed in Log In Forgot your password? Don't have an account? Sign Up (New