led Category: Curriculum and Instruction ; +1 Teacher Education Adjunct Instructor – Global Education Certificate in Teacher Continuing Education University of Haiti–Elms College Training Partnership Elms College is seeking an experienced and collaborative Adjunct Instructor to teach Curriculum Design , a 3-credit course within the Certificate in Teacher Continuing Education , offered through a collaborative teacher education partnership between Elms College and the University of Haiti . This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to an international teacher education initiative designed to strengthen teachers' knowledge and skills in curriculum development, instructional planning, and effective educational practice. Position Overview The selected instructor will teach the same 12-week course to two cohorts of approximately 25 teachers each . The course will be delivered synchronously online via Zoom and co-taught with an instructor from the University of Haiti . The course is scheduled to begin in mid-December 2026 and continue through the first week of March 2027 . The instructor will teach: Cohort 1: Tuesdays, synchronous Zoom Cohort 2: Thursdays, synchronous Zoom Class length: Approximately 2½ hours per session Course length: 12 weeks Enrollment: Approximately 25 students per cohort Course: Curriculum Design (3 credits) The instructor will teach the same course content and learning outcomes to both cohorts , while adapting examples, activities, and discussions to the needs and experiences of participating teachers. Responsibilities The Adjunct Instructor will: Collaboratively plan and co-teach Curriculum Design with a University of Haiti faculty member. Facilitate engaging, interactive synchronous Zoom sessions focused on curriculum development and instructional planning. Introduce teachers to principles and practices of effective curriculum design. Connect curriculum theory and research to teachers' classroom experiences and educational contexts. Engage teachers in analyzing curriculum, developing learning objectives, selecting instructional strategies, and designing meaningful learning experiences. Incorporate culturally responsive and contextually relevant approaches to curriculum development. Design learning activities that encourage collaboration, reflection, problem-solving, and practical application. Provide clear expectations and timely feedback on student assignments and projects. Work collaboratively with the University of Haiti co-instructor to ensure consistency in course delivery, assessment, and student support. Communicate regularly with program leadership and the co-instructor regarding student progress and course needs. Support an inclusive online learning environment that recognizes the varied teaching experiences and educational backgrounds of participating teachers. Qualifications Required: Master's degree in Education, Curriculum and Instruction, Teacher Education, Educational Leadership, or a closely related field. Demonstrated experience in curriculum design, curriculum development, instructional planning, or a related area. Experience teaching educators, teachers, or adult learners. Experience teaching in an online or synchronous virtual environment. Fluency in English. Strong interpersonal, communication, and collaborative skills. Preferred: Doctorate in Education or a related field. Proficiency in French and/or Haitian Creole . Experience working in international, multicultural, or cross-cultural education settings. Experience working with teachers or educational professionals in Haiti or other international contexts. Experience co-teaching or collaborating with faculty from another institution or educational system. Knowledge of culturally responsive curriculum development and adult learning. Experience designing professional development for practicing educators. Appointment and Compensation This is a part-time adjunct faculty appointment through Elms College . The selected instructor will be compensated according to Elms College's adjunct faculty compensation structure. Because the instructor will teach two cohorts of the same course, the position includes teaching responsibilities for two sections of the 3-credit course . $6,000 stipend. Application Interested candidates should submit: A current curriculum vitae or résumé A brief cover letter describing their qualifications and interest in teaching Curriculum Design as part of this international teacher education partnership Contact information for two professional references Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Anticipated course dates: Mid-December 2026 through the first week of March 2027 Course format: Synchronous online (Zoom) Course duration: 12 weeks Cohorts: Two cohorts of approximately 25 students Institution: Elms College, in partnership with the University of Haiti Elms College (also known as College of Our Lady of the Elms), a private, Catholic, co-educational liberal arts institution in Chicopee, Massachusetts, was founded in 1928 by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Springfield. The institution offers Associate's, Bachelor's, Master's, and Doctor of Nursing practice degrees. Dedicated to non-discriminatory educational practices, the College aims to eliminate barriers to equal access and treatment for its community. Elms College provides rigorous academic challenges and fosters a supportive community for students to thrive. Graduates leave Elms College richer, rooted in faith, educated, compassionate, responsive to civic and social obligations, and capable of adjusting to change without compromising principle. Elms College’s mission embodies the charism of the founders, the Sisters of St. Joseph, including embracing “the love of neighbor without distinction” and whose Catholic heritage guides our intellectual, social, educational, and community endeavors. Elms College is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants will not be discriminated against because of race, color, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, national origin, citizenship status, disability, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, medical condition, or any protected category prohibited by local, state or federal laws. Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the U.S.. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Apply Now Related Searches: Curriculum and Instruction Teacher Education Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Email: jobs@elms.edu OR Apply through HigherEdJobs Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) Post Doctorate Adjunct/Part-Time Administrative/Staff Executive (Director, Asst/Assoc VP/Dean) Senior Executive (VP, Dean, President/Chancellor) Please type the characters to the left above (case sensitive). Close Job Seeker Login Email Password Keep me signed in Log I