    "https://www.higheredjobs.com/institution/details.cfm?JobCode=179550930&Title=Slate%20Enrollment%20Communications%20Administrator": {
      "title": "Slate Enrollment Communications Administrator",
      "description": "Slate Enrollment Communications Administrator - HigherEdJobs Your Privacy We use cookies and other similar technologies to enhance user experience, for website maintenance purposes, and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our website with advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal, then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Do Not Sell My Personal Information I understand Skip to main content Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Online/Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail Slate Enrollment Communications Administrator Elms College in Chicopee, MA Apply Now Type: Full-Time Salary: $70,000 - $75,000 per year Posted: 35 days ago Application Due: Open Until Filled Category: Communications, Marketing, and Public Affairs ; +1 Admissions and Enrollment Reports to: VP of Enrollment Management and Marketing Position Summary The Slate Enrollment Communications Administrator is responsible for developing and executing comprehensive communications for undergraduate and graduate admissions and supporting the effective use and continued development of the College’s Slate CRM instance. This position combines strong writing and communication strategy with advanced Slate knowledge to create timely, accurate, personalized, and engaging communications throughout the student recruitment and enrollment journey. The Administrator serves as the primary writer for first-year, transfer, continuing education, and graduate admissions communications and works closely with enrollment, marketing, and other campus partners to ensure messaging is audience-focused, consistent with the College’s brand, and aligned with institutional enrollment goals. The position also oversees the development and maintenance of Slate communications, portals, forms, events, workflows, and other recruitment-related functionality. Essential Responsibilities Develop, write, edit, and execute communications for prospective students, applicants, admitted students, deposited students, families, school counselors, and other enrollment audiences. Serve as the primary writer for undergraduate and graduate admissions communications, including email campaigns, text messages, letters, application and enrollment instructions, event communications, and other recruitment materials. Create communication plans that support students throughout the enrollment funnel, from inquiry through enrollment. Adapt messaging appropriately for undergraduate, graduate, transfer, continuing education, international, and other priority populations. Ensure communications are clear, engaging, accurate, student-centered, and consistent with the College’s brand, voice, and enrollment priorities. Partner with Undergraduate Admissions, Graduate Admissions, Financial Aid, Marketing and Communications, and other campus offices to gather information and coordinate messaging. Maintain an enrollment communications calendar and manage communication timelines, approvals, testing, and deployment. Review existing communications regularly and recommend improvements based on enrollment priorities, student needs, engagement data, and industry best practices. Support the development of segmented and personalized communication strategies for different student populations and stages of the enrollment process. Proofread and quality-check communications for content, grammar, formatting, links, personalization, audience criteria, and accuracy prior to deployment. Monitor communication performance and use engagement and conversion data to improve future outreach. Support the administration, optimization, and continued development of Slate for undergraduate and graduate enrollment. Build, manage, and maintain Slate Deliver campaigns, including recipient populations, segmentation, personalization, liquid markup, templates, scheduling, and testing. Develop and maintain Slate portals. Create and update portal content, displays, interactions, checklists, status information, and personalized student experiences. Build and maintain Slate forms, events, registrations, landing pages, queries, reports, filters, rules, and automated workflows. Support application configuration, applicant status communications, decision release processes, enrollment checklists, and other admission-related functions. Assist with reporting and analysis related to communication engagement, recruitment activity, funnel progression, and enrollment outcomes. Ensure that Slate communications and processes comply with institutional policies and applicable privacy and accessibility standards. Participate in enrollment planning meetings and contribute to recruitment, communication, and yield strategies. Assist with major enrollment initiatives, recruitment events, and special projects. Collaborate with campus partners to support coordinated and consistent communications to prospective and incoming students. Stay current on enrollment communication trends, Slate best practices, and emerging technologies. Perform other duties as assigned, which may include evening or weekend events. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Three or more years of experience in enrollment communications, admissions operations, CRM administration, or a related are preferred. Demonstrated professional experience using Slate CRM. Working knowledge of HTML and CSS. Strong writing, editing, and proofreading skills, with the ability to communicate clearly and effectively with varied audiences. Strong attention to detail and commitment to thorough testing and quality assurance. Ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with colleagues across departments. Experience handling confidential information with discretion and sound judgment. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to build productive relationships with both technical and nontechnical colleagues. Elms College (also known as College of Our Lady of the Elms), a private, Catholic, co-educational liberal arts institution in Chicopee, Massachusetts, was founded in 1928 by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Springfield. The institution offers Associate's, Bachelor's, Master's, and Doctor of Nursing practice degrees. Dedicated to non-discriminatory educational practices, the College aims to eliminate barriers to equal access and treatment for its community. Elms College provides rigorous academic challenges and fosters a supportive community for students to thrive. Graduates leave Elms College richer, rooted in faith, educated, compassionate, responsive to civic and social obligations, and capable of adjusting to change without compromising principle. Elms College’s mission embodies the charism of the founders, the Sisters of St. Joseph, including embracing “the love of neighbor without distinction” and whose Catholic heritage guides our intellectual, social, educational, and community endeavors. Elms College is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants will not be discriminated against because of race, color, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, national origin, citizenship status, disability, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, medical condition, or any protected category prohibited by local, state or federal laws. Apply Now Related Searches: Communications, Marketing, and Public Affairs Admissions and Enrollment Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Email: jobs@elms.edu OR Apply through HigherEdJobs Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) 