    "https://www.higheredjobs.com/institution/details.cfm?JobCode=179543310&Title=Gift%20Processor%20%28Part%2DTime%29": {
      "title": "Gift Processor (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Gift Processor (Part-Time) - HigherEdJobs Your Privacy We use cookies and other similar technologies to enhance user experience, for website maintenance purposes, and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our website with advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal, then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Do Not Sell My Personal Information I understand Skip to main content Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Online/Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail Gift Processor (Part-Time) Elms College in Chicopee, MA Apply Now Type: Adjunct/Part-Time Salary: $18 per hour Posted: 44 days ago (Reposted Job: Initially posted on 06/08/2026) Application Due: Open Until Filled Category: Development and Fundraising ; +1 Alumni Relations Job Summary: The Gift Processor manages the administrative functions of the advancement office, i.e. accounting,gift recording, and database management. Highly detail oriented with a critical degree of accuracyregarding data entry and analysis; good interpersonal and organizational skills; ability to prioritizework and adhere to deadline, good problem-solving and analytical skills; ability to take responsibility,work well as a team member and to work independently; ability to understand and follow directionsand complex policies and procedures; ability to deal with confidential data. Supervisory Responsibilities: May supervise student workers. Duties/Responsibilities: • Ensures that al! pledges and gifts and event payments to the College are processed and receipted accurately and on a timely basis by managing the daily work of gifts processing and pledge management in the Institutional Advancement database (currently Raiser\"sEdge). Responsible for the data Integrity and maintaining the confidentiality of that data. Processes all credit card gifts. • Runs daily proof reports for each gift batch and completing deposit slips for daily entries, accuracy of the data ls subject to audit. Reviews and analyzes data problems. May handle donor inquiries and issues directly. • Creates new gift designations accurately in the database and maintains files and statements of Intent. • Produces gift receipts and individualized acknowledgement letters for all gifts received ln a timely and accurate fashion. Generates outstanding pledge reports and sends pledge reminders quarterly. • Manages Tribute program, which includes tribute acknowledgement to donors and next of kln/tributee. • Works with Business Office, Advancement staff and other departments of the College to communicate relevant procedures relating to the processing of donations and provides them with financial reports. • Enters and maintains biographical information In the Advancement database, including creating new entity records for alumni, individuals, organizations and corporations, and updating existing records. Responsible for the Integrity of this data. • Organizes, coordinates and maintains the integrity of the hard copy filing systems. • Trains and manages student staff when appropriate and necessary. • Assists Business Office In yearly audit by providing reports and proof of gifts and pledges. • Assists Director of Advancement Services with special projects and requests. • Contacts donors for gift clarification when necessary. • May require some evening and weekend hours. • May require holiday or office closure hours. • Other duties as may be assigned. Required Skills/Abilities: • Strong computer skills including MS Word, Excel, and database entry and reporting 3Xperience. • Detail oriented and ability to handle multiple detailed tasks. • Good interpersonal and organizational skills. • Ability to interact with donors and other departments. Education and Experience: • Associates degree required, bachelor's degree preferred. • Experience in an office environment. • Knowledge of automated systems, including databases, spreadsheets, report formats. Experience with maintaining confidential records. • Knowledge and understanding of financial, statistical, or administrative record-keeping techniques. • Knowledge of general office procedures and practices sufficient to input, maintain, retrieve and distribute information. Physical Requirements: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. • Use of general office equipment in an office setting. Requires an equal amount of standing, sitting,walking, bending, stooping, reaching, climbing multiple levels of stairs, light lifting, near vision and manual dexterity to perform essential job functions. Requires ability to travel between buildings on campus with exposure to inclement weather conditions. • May require driving or traveling to locations in the local and outside the local area on official college business. • Background check will be conducted upon hire and on a routine basis thereafter. • Valid driver's license and good driving record required. Elms College (also known as College of Our Lady of the Elms), a private, Catholic, co- educational liberal arts institution in Chicopee, Massachusetts, was founded in 1928 by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Springfield. The institution offers Associate's, Bachelor's, Master's, and Doctor of Nursing practice degrees. Dedicated to non-discriminatory educational practices, the College aims to eliminate barriers to equal access and treatment for its community. Elms College provides rigorous academic challenges and fosters a supportive community for students to thrive. Graduates leave Elms College richer, rooted in faith, educated, compassionate, responsive to civic and social obligations, and capable of adjusting to change without compromising principle. Elms College’s mission embodies the charism of the founders, the Sisters of St. Joseph, including embracing “the love of neighbor without distinction” and whose Catholic heritage guides our intellectual, social, educational, and community endeavors. Elms College is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants will not be discriminated against because of race, color, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, religion, national origin, citizenship status, disability, ancestry, marital status, veteran status, medical condition, or any protected category prohibited by local, state or federal laws. Apply Now Related Searches: Development and Fundraising Alumni Relations Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Email: jobs@elms.edu OR Apply through HigherEdJobs Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) Post Doctorate Adjunct/Part-Time Administrative/Staff Executive (Director, Asst/Assoc VP/Dean) Senior Executive (VP, Dean, President/Chancellor) Please type the characters to the left above (case sensitive). Close Job Seeker Login Email Password Keep me signed in Log In Forgot your password? Don't have an account? Sign Up (New) Terms and Conditions of Use (Updated) Privacy Policy"
